'''''Rotadiscus''''' is a genus of discoidal animal known from the Cambrian [[Chengjiang biota]]<ref>{{harvnb|Zhu|Zhao|Chen|2002}}</ref> and classified with the [[eldonioid]]s.<ref name=Caron2010>{{harvnb|Caron|Conway Morris|Shu|Soares|2010}}</ref>

As with other eldonioids, it was originally thought to have been pelagic, but is now thought to be benthic.

A 2023 cladistic analysis based on new fossils places ''Rotadiscus'', along with other eldonioids, as stem-group [[ambulacraria]]ns in the clade [[Cambroernida]].<ref name="li2023">{{harvnb|Li|Dunn|Murdock|Guo|2023}}</ref>

